te in eu  pro league  my source who requested to remain  anonymous provided a translated version  of the conversation  in which jeremy asks another player if  they'd be willing to throw an upcoming  gsa match against  rogue the other person in the  conversation basically asks if jeremy's  suggesting that they match fix  and share me replies yes from there  cheremy doubles down and says that this  match against rogue isn't important to  the other team  and that rogue winning would help devise  and get closer to clinching that  challenger league  spot remember as an amateur team you  don't even have to win  gsa you just have to be the highest  ranked amateur team  in the league so you can imagine winning  the gsa league would be a huge step  up for an amateur team like devising  from there we were told that the player  talking to jeremy got in touch with his  general manager  and they went back and forth as to  whether or not they should report this  incident to ubisoft  soon after that our source told us that  the player talking to cherymy  was contacted by another siege player in  the gsa  and they said that cheremy had allegedly  done this before  in something called the saturday league  and the saturday league is basically  another amateur league that players can  compete  in it was after hearing that ceremony  had allegedly done this before  that the person talking to share me  decided to file a report to ubisoft  now i talked to shermy and he says that  he eventually heard that ubisoft was  looking to ban him because of this  conversation so he went to the person  that he had the conversation with  and said hey man i was just joking can  you tell ubisoft that  according to shareme there was no match  fixing here it was all just a joke but  eventually ubisoft handed cheremy a  six-month ban  that ends in january of 2021 ubisoft  germany eventually made a statement  about this  and translated it reads quote as a  result of an investigation because of  attempted match fixing while playing in  the 2020 version of the gsa league  we decided to ban cheremy from team  devison for the next six months  from all esport competitions end quote  now after the ban was announced  jeremy doubled down on social media  saying that he wasn't serious about  match fixing and that it was all a joke  and he also thinks that he probably  won't be able to come back from this  and like i said i talked to him about  this situation and here's what he had to  say about the ban  and i messaged him like yay why don't  you throw the same way that you did  today against like  uh rogue on the on the last match day  and then he said like yeah  uh is this match fixing what you want  for me and i was like yes  ha ha ha ha like like like choking  around  like at this moment like i never  expected like  him or like anyone to like take  screenshots of this conversation and  then just  send it to ubisoft like a day or two  days later  uh ubisoft contacted devising the orc i  played for  and told them that i am like locked and  i'm not allowed to play it till like  they know what happened there now the  response to cheremy's ban  online is largely in his favor some  people are calling  six months too harsh and other people  are wondering why he got  banned at all since he didn't actually  match fix  now you have to imagine that cheremy  attempting to match fix  is what led ubisoft to give him a  six-month ban if he  actually matched fixed the punishment  would be much worse and shermy says that  he was pulled into a conference call  with ubisoft executives  and they said that hey you can tell us  your story but it's not going to affect  the ban  you're still getting a six-month ban no  matter what happens  we have like a phone call with like uh  the german ubisoft center and there were  like three people in it i don't know who  they're all in but it was like the head  chef from the german office  yeah like two other guys and they the  first thing they told me like  yeah decision is already done you can  tell us your  story now but it wouldn't affect the  outcome and when it comes to the  allegation that shami attempted to match  fix in that amateur  saturday league he says that never  happened  no i never did anything like that and i  don't know what he even said  like even him said it you tried this  before and i asked him what do you mean  but i  like hands down it's where i'm alive i  never like  did like any match fixing in any league  with this chat that i was with him  it's not even match fixing i didn't even  gave him anything like normal match  fixing would be like oh yeah i give you  money and you  you throw your game or something like  that it was just purely chat  i don't even know how like they are  managing to say like oh yeah  your career is now over and you get  banned for six months like i don't  understand  now i don't know if jeremy was serious  or if he was just joking but what i do  know  is that you probably shouldn't slide  into the dms of somebody you don't know  that well  and say hey wanna do some match fixing i  mean why even give ubisoft the chance to  slam down that band hammer  critics of cheremy point to pengu who  makes jokes about match fixing on social  media implying that if pengu can do it  why can't share me well to be honest  there's a big difference between a tweet  that everyone can publicly see  and a dm conversation one you never  match fix  in public and two it's much harder to  tell if someone's joking when they slide  into your dms  look i have no idea if shermy was  serious or not and i have no idea if  this ban is too harsh  but i do know that if you want to be a  pro player joking about match fixing  online it's probably not a good idea  colton has just been talking about the  fact that his legs have been giving him  issues over the last couple of months  and he doesn't know why  and my old ass there are days when i get  out of bed  and i [ __ ] tweak something in my back  and that's it for me  i'm 25 years old and i have these  [ __ ] problems i don't know what's  happening  should probably see somebody about it i  have no excuse  i have no excuse i'm doing ymca now  i have no [ __ ] excuse

